# build/ is NOT ignored. It is the prerendered site RUN-DEMO.bat serves, and committing it is what
# lets a clone run the demo with nothing but Python — no Node, no npm install, no network. It is
# generated, so it can go stale: `npm run verify` rebuilds it, and any frontend change should be
# committed together with the rebuild it produces.
